[948.196718, "o", "print(tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True))\r\n\" 2>&1 — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash python3 -c \" from peft import PeftModel from transformers import AutoM…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 34 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ The adapter loads and generates responses. Let me also verify the trainin…\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 35 tool call(s) so far\r\n  qwen3.6-35b — 36 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ read /app/train_lora.py\r\n    ✓ read /app/train_lora.py — 160 lines\r\n  ⚙ todo \r\n    ✓ todo — 5/5 done\r\nAll tasks complete. Here's a summary:\r\n\r\n**What was done:**\r\n\r\n1. **Installed dependencies**: `torch`, `transformers`, `peft==0.15.0`, `accelerate`, `datasets`, `safetensors`, `trl`\r\n\r\n2. **Created `/app/train_lora.py`**: Training script that:\r\n   - Loads `openai-community/gpt2` as the base model\r\n   - Applies LoRA with `r=8`, `alpha=16`, targeting `c_attn` modules\r\n   - Formats each sample as a causal-LM prompt: `Question: ... Options: ... Answer: ...`\r\n   - Trains for 5 epochs with batch size 8"]
[948.208948, "o", ", gradient accumulation 2, LR 5e-4\r\n   - Saves the LoRA adapter and tokenizer to `/app/experiments/lora_adapter/`\r\n   - Writes results to `/app/lora_results.json`\r\n\r\n3. **Training completed** (5 epochs, ~10 min/epoch, total ~611s):\r\n   - Eval loss dropped from 2.5 → 2.081\r\n   - Trainable parameters: 294,912 (0.24% of total)\r\n\r\n4. **Output files verified:**\r\n   - `/app/train_lora.py` — training script\r\n   - `/app/experiments/lora_adapter/adapter_config.json` — has `base_model_name_or_path` and `task_type`\r\n   - `/app/experiments/lora_adapter/adapter_model.safetensors` — LoRA weights (1.2 MB)\r\n   - `/app/experiments/lora_adapter/tokenizer_config.json` — tokenizer config\r\n   - `/app/lora_results.json` — matches required schema exactly\r\n\r\n5. **Adapter loads and generates responses** — tested successfully with a biomedical QA prompt.\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=qwen3.6-35b tools=36 surface=48cd0ade3676\r\n"]
